  "quote": "The grinding circuit consists of a two‐stage ball mill combination which is well suited to handling the variable hardness expected from mixtures of the high‐silica copper stockwork material and the softer massive sulphide rock. The grinding circuit is designed to reduce the particle size of flotation feed slurry to a nominal 80% ‐75µm as indicated by recent metallurgical testwork. Cyclone overflow slurry from the secondary mill would be directed to the flotation section for sequential copper/lead and zinc concentrate recovery.",
  "page": 39
 },
